The vsock port the master reaches the guest daemon on, for the status, the
config and the actions of the encap instances, with no network and no
credential. Set to `0` to not use it.

The guest needs a vsock device, as `<vsock model='virtio'><cid auto='yes'/></vsock>`
in the domain definition, and to serve the port with its `listener.vsock_port`
keyword. When the guest daemon does not answer on it, the master uses the `qga`
or the `rcmd` way, so this keyword needs no change when a guest has no device.
